+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+With `transport.history.enabled`, a client MAY request its authenticated user's conversations by
+sending `list_conversations`. `limit`, when present, is an integer from 1 through 200. `before`,
+when present, contains both the ISO-string `updatedAt` and string `sessionId` from the last summary
+seen. The server accepts this frame independently of whether history is enabled.
+
+The server answers on the connection's authenticated user id, never a value supplied in the frame,
+and forwards `limit` and `before` to the session store. It answers outside the per-session turn lock.
+([validated by: answers from the authenticated user in newest-first wire form and pages with the returned cursor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L145))
+
+Malformed limits or cursors receive `INVALID_MESSAGE`. ([validated by: validates the list frame and its bounded composite cursor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L111))
 
 ## 5. Server-to-Client Messages
 
+### 5.0 conversation_list
+
+A successful request receives exactly one `conversation_list`, with no `stream_end`. Its
+`conversations` are newest first and each row contains `sessionId`, `entryCount`, and ISO-string
+`createdAt` and `updatedAt`; it contains no conversation content. If history is disabled or the
+store cannot list, the server sends an `error` with code `UNSUPPORTED`, never a misleading empty
+list. ([validated by: reports UNSUPPORTED instead of an empty list when history is disabled or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L175))
+
